From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:00:53 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 16/45] inkling2: the image path (processor, vision tower,
 placeholder splice)

The image processor runs on the host: PNG, JPEG or WebP through main's
decoders, EXIF orientation, alpha over the processor's checkerboard, then
-1 padding to the 40-pixel grid and (v - 127.5) / 127.5 in fp32, one token
per 40 x 40 cell with no resize. Its pixel_values are byte-equal to
Inkling2ImageProcessor on seven test pictures.

The tower runs on one GPU in bf16 over main's vit helpers plus four
family kernels (vision.cu): patch embedding, the 32 x 32 position table
resampled bilinearly, class token, 23 layers with 2D rotary and layer
scale, then proj_in, GELU and proj_out to 4608. Its rows match the
transformers bf16 tower within the gap between that tower and its own
fp32 run; with rotary turned off the cosine drops to 0.65-0.96.

vision.spans/check/splice give the decoder hook: after the normed
embedding of a pass, the rows at placeholder positions take the image
rows in prompt order, as masked_scatter does, for any prompt chunking.
tf-inkling2-vision writes the processor output, the tower rows and a
spliced prompt for the check against the reference.
